    "Virus Executable File",
    "3.6",
    "Executable file that contains a virus; renamed from.EXE to .vexe, where v stands for virus; may have been renamed manually or by an antivirus program; may have been distributed through malware programs on infected computers. NOTE: If you have a VEXE file on your system, it is recommended that you scan the file using and antivirus program. Windows An antivirus program.",
